    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d481">

                <pb facs="1177" n="1063" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg1063"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt and
                        Prime Minister Churchill to Marshal Stalin
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d481-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">most secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            
                                <hi rendition="#small-caps">Quadrant</hi>
                            </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-19">19
                            August 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>President and Prime Minister to Marshal Stalin. Most Secret and Personal.</p>
                <p>Reference our immediately preceding telegram.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d481-f2"/>
                </p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Operation referred to in paragraph 1 is attack on West Coast of Italian
                        mainland. Code name in paragraph 3 refers to Portuguese Atlantic
                        islands.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Following instructions to General Eisenhower referred to in paragraph 2.
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Begins:</hi> (Here insert paraphrased text of
                            
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fan</hi>
                         196<anchor n="3" xml:id="d481-f3"/>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Ends</hi>.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d481-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d481-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the War Cabinet Office in London as Churchill’s telegram No. 
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welfare</hi>
                     218 and forwarded to the British Ambassador in the Soviet Union (Clark
                    Kerr). Concerning the delivery of this message in Moscow, see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg1062">p. 1062</ref>, fn.
                    1.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d481-f2" n="2" xml:id="d481-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d481-f3" n="3" xml:id="d481-f3-content">
                <p>For the text of telegram No. 
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fan</hi>
                     196 as dispatched from Quebec on August 18, 1943, see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg1060">p. 1060</ref>. For the
                    paraphrased text of this telegram as included in the message delivered to
                    Stalin, see <hi rendition="#italic">Stalin’s Correspondence</hi>, vol. <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, pp. 144–146; vol. <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, pp. 80–82.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
